@startuml
title Dietary update: successful repair with existing groceries
autonumber
participant "command: SetDietCommand" as C
participant "activePlan: ActiveMealPlan" as A
participant "planner: DietaryPlanner" as P
participant "groceries: GroceryListGenerator" as G
participant "settings: DietarySettings" as S
[-> C : execute(recipeBook)
activate C
C -> A : get()
A --> C : currentPlan present
C -> P : isCompatible(currentPlan, preferences)
P --> C : false
C -> A : getRequest()
A --> C : originalRequest present
C -> P : repair(recipes, currentPlan, originalRequest, preferences)
activate P
note over P
  Count conflicting days.
  generate() filters eligible recipes and delegates to MealPlanGenerator.
  Reuse compatible days in their original positions.
end note
P --> C : updatedPlan
deactivate P
C -> A : getGroceryList()
A --> C : existing snapshot present
create G
C -> G : new GroceryListGenerator()
C -> G : generateForPlan(updatedPlan)
G --> C : rebuilt groceries
C -> A : setGenerated(updatedPlan, originalRequest, groceries)
C -> S : set(preferences)
C -->[ : saved and repaired confirmation
deactivate C
legend bottom
  Successful conflicting-plan branch only. RecipeBook getter and Optional operations are condensed.
  If repair throws IllegalArgumentException, save preferences, clear active state, and return an explanation.
  No-plan and already-compatible branches are described in the guide.
endlegend
@enduml
